    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks passed.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: the instance girder section had t_top = 0.20 m, contradicting the description (\"top slab 0.18 m thick\"). The accepted section-derived decisions (A, I, w, m) had been computed for t_top = 0.18, so the model's member parameters did not reproduce their provenance decisions — the L2-1 recomputation check failed. I corrected the instance to t_top = 0.18 m (full section written, since the merge requires all geometry fields), which invalidated and required re-deciding girder.single.A/I, girder.A/I, girder.w, girder.m, and lane.mu.\n\nModel summary:\n- Single simply supported span, 25 m bearing centre lines; deck 16 m wide, one-way, carriageway 15 m, 4 lanes.\n- Spine-beam 2D idealization; 5 precast prestressed small-box girders per span merged into one spine (MR-02).\n- Single girder section (integrated): A = 1.0605 m², I = 0.25166 m⁴; merged: A = 5.3026 m², I = 1.25829 m⁴.\n- C40 concrete, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³; self-weight only: w = 137.87 kN/m, m = 14.054 t/m (MR-07).\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric, 2 per girder end × 5 girders = 10 per line at both abutments; per-bearing S = 10.096, Kv = 1.4163e7 kN/m, Kh = 3.281e4 kN/m for the line.\n- Live load: Highway Class II, 4 design lanes, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 232.5 kN, ξ = 0.67; impact μ = 0.2409 from f1 = 4.272 Hz (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nKey results: f1 = 4.272 Hz (vertical bending); self-weight support reactions 1723.3 kN each; self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kN·m; lane live-load max positive moment 6878.4 kN·m at midspan."
